      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The absolute value equation $|n + 6| = 2 - n$ implies two cases: $n + 6 \\geq 0$ and $n + 6 < 0$.\n\nWhen $n + 6 \\geq 0$, the equation becomes $n + 6 = 2 - n$.\nThe solution follows from this equation.\nSolving this, we find $n = -\\frac{4}{2} = -2$.\n\nWhen $n + 6 < 0$, the equation becomes $-(n + 6) = 2 - n$.\nThe solution follows from this equation.\nSolving this, we find $n = -\\frac{8}{2} = -4$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is $n \\in \\boxed{-4, -2}$.",
