    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "\\begin{align*}\nn &\\geq 0 \\quad \\text{(when $n + 6$ is positive or zero, or when $2 - n$ is positive or zero)}\\\\\nn &\\leq 2 \\quad \\text{(when $n + 6$ is negative, or when $2 - n$ is negative)}\n\\end{align*}Since $0 \\leq n \\leq 2$, we can square both sides of each inequality: \\begin{align*}\nn^2 &\\geq 0\\\\\nn^2 &\\leq 4\n\\end{align*}Finally, since $n^2 \\geq n$, we can square both sides of the original equation: \\begin{align*}\nn^2 + 12n + 36 &= 4 - 4n + n^2\\\\\n16n &=- 32\\\\\nn &= \\boxed{-2}\n\\end{align*}. The answer is -2",
