    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "First, because $2 - n \\ge 0$, so if the equation holds, then $n \\le 2$.\n\nSecond, we need to find the roots of $|n + 6| = 2 - n$.\n\nCase 1: $n + 6 \\ge 0$.\nIn this case, $|n + 6| = n + 6$, so the equation becomes $n + 6 = 2 - n$. Solving for $n$ yields $n = -2$.\n\nCase 2: $n + 6 < 0$.\nIn this case, $|n + 6| = -(n + 6) = -n - 6$, so the equation becomes $-n - 6 = 2 - n$. Solving for $n$ yields $n = -8$.\n\nSince both $-2$ and $-8$ are within the unit $[0, 2]$, the answer is $\\boxed{-8, -2}$.",
